    lessonPlan: '0–5 Story wall: one word from each chapter on the board, prediction of the ending; 5–12 Listen for the task, then read along; 12–18 Pairs complete a four-box chart (task / promise / today / message) with sentences from the text, whole-class check; 18–22 Quick Challenge; 22–31 Language Focus: Activity 1 as whole-class discovery (past or future? sure or not?), Activity 2 as a question game where you point to a part of the sentence and learners call out When?, Where?, How often? or Why?, Activity 3 in pairs; 31–37 Use: groups choose a real shared class task (a class library, a clean-up day) and write four sentences with will … for sure, to + verb, After and still; 37–40 Exit ticket and a short preview of the whole-book review pages.',
    discussionPoints: ['What task did Allah give Abraham?', 'How did Ishmael answer his father?', 'What does the chapter say Hajj helps people remember?', 'What is Abraham’s message?'],
